  "scope": [
    "Turn the current Dashboard shell into a Temple management console whose Now view is the operational dashboard, and add an always-visible Organization view backed by canonical Agent Identity, Position, Assignment, membership, and collaboration-profile data."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Navigation and copy present the surface as a management console; Now remains the operational Dashboard and Organization is a distinct primary destination.",
    "Organization renders all active Agent Identities and all ten assigned Positions even when no Work Item is actively claimed, with Agent-centric and Position-centric views and clear responsibilities.",
    "Organization exposes the current collaboration profile and visible separation safeguards without conflating permanent organization topology with current execution.",
    "Execution remains scoped to current claimed, blocked, or live-attached work and preserves Agent to Position to Work Item to Codex task to observed model mapping.",
    "The implementation uses shadcn-inspired composition and density without adding or copying the shadcn dependency, preserves private-viewer redaction and mutation boundaries, and works at desktop, tablet, and mobile widths.",
    "A repository-backed requirements audit distinguishes shipped, partial, planned, and intentionally deferred control-plane capabilities; focused tests, full verification, and independent browser QA pass on an exact candidate."
  ],
